    note: "The apex arc one grid step above C10's minimum. The first candidate whose counter clears 1 unit both ways at 16. Apex: apex drawn as an arc of radius 0.75 (C10's minimum at this master is 0.625), circular, so (rx − stroke/2)/(ry − stroke/2) = 1.00. Ink 24 · 20 · 16: 8×8.25 · 6×6.25 · 5×5.25 — the brief's 8.25 · 6.25 · 5.25 of height at every master, the same in both styles, centred (0.125 high at 24 and 20, where a truly centred ink box would need a 3-dp centreline). Letter width over height at 16: 0.95. Legs 20.8 · 17.8 · 18.4 degrees off vertical. Crossbar at 38% of the centreline height above the baseline (y 8.5 at 16), ends landing on the leg centrelines. SILHOUETTE: the bar shows 0 past the legs' outer edges at every master, measured by walking the ink outward from each leg centreline at 128 samples per unit. A round cap of radius half the stroke lies entirely inside a stroke of the same width exactly when its centre is on or inside that stroke's centreline, so the bar's ends land ON the leg centrelines, rounded INWARD at the last decimal place — that is the longest bar with an unbroken outer line down each leg. APEX COUNTER at 16, flood-filled on the drawing itself: 1.02×1.25 (w:h 0.82, area 0.75); at 20 1.31×1.5, at 24 2.44×2.75. The counter is a taper, so its width over its height is fixed by the splay alone — 2·tan(leg angle) on every candidate here — and the crossbar height sets only how much of it there is. FILLED: a real solid letterform, not a thickened wire. Its outer edge is the outline drawing's own outer edge point for point — the same leg edges, the same apex arc at radius r + half a stroke, the same round feet — and the counter is CUT AS A HOLE, so it keeps its air however heavy the letter gets. Extra weight goes where the counter never pays for it: the crossbar is deepened downward by 0.5 · 0.25 · 0.375 and the legs are pulled in below it by 0.5 · 0.25 · 0.25 — only as far as leaves 1.5 of air in the notch between them, which is why the narrow candidates get less or none. Notch after thickening 2.95 · 1.94 · 1.6. Counter neck (the narrowest span facing itself square-on, the repo's own facingGap, which is what lint §5f reads): clear · 1.26 · 0.96 — under §6's 1.5, so lint warns; that warning IS this study's question restated, and the outline twin has exactly the same counter and is not measured only because §5b's turn gate never fires on a two-legged path.",
